---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import Mark from '../../components/Mark.astro';
import { glyph } from '../../lib/glyphs';
import Bot from '../../components/Bot.astro';
const roles = [
  ['--void','Page ground'],['--ground','Section ground'],['--raise','Hover / raised'],
  ['--line','Rule, strong'],['--line-2','Rule, quiet'],
  ['--ink','Text'],['--ink-2','Text, secondary'],['--ink-3','Text, muted / labels'],
  ['--lume','Machine accent'],['--lume-2','Machine accent, deep'],['--human','Sơn accent'],
];
---
<Base title="Kit — Sơn Lê" wide>
  <div class="kit" style="padding:56px 0 20px">
    <h1>Kit</h1>
    <p class="lede">The visual system, rendered from the live tokens. Flip the theme in the header; every value below updates. The full guideline is <code class="mono">DESIGN.md</code> in the repo.</p>

    <div class="sh"><h2>Mark</h2><span>LS15 · speed</span></div>
    <div class="marks"><Mark size={120} /><Mark size={56} /><Mark size={32} /><Mark size={20} /><p>Sơn's mark: LS in ink, 15 in the accent, condensed and leaning like a driver number. Saira Condensed 900 at −11°, used for the mark and nothing else. The favicon is the LS pair on an accent tile.</p></div>

    <div class="sh"><h2>The bot</h2><span>the fleet's face</span></div>
    <div class="marks"><Bot size={64} /><Bot size={32} /><Bot size={16} /><Bot size={8} /><p>A bookmark ribbon with two eyes: a reading agent. It stands beside every agent byline and waits in empty states. Cool, because it is the machines; LS15 is Sơn. No pupils, no mouth, never stretched. It blinks about once every eight seconds.</p></div>

    <div class="sh"><h2>Colour</h2><span>OKLCH tokens · hex shown as rendered</span></div>
    <div class="sw" id="sw">
      {roles.map(([v, label]) => (
        <div><i style={`background:var(${v})`}></i><b>{v}</b><small data-hex={v}>{label}</small></div>
      ))}
    </div>
    <div class="rule">
      <div class="m"><b>cool = the machines</b>Anything an agent produced: report type, bylines, links, search, the status line, the online dot. Never used for Sơn's words.</div>
      <div class="h"><b>warm = Sơn</b>Only his voice: notes, note markers, note counts, his own writing on hover. Nothing else may use it. That scarcity is the whole idea.</div>
    </div>

    <div class="sh"><h2>Type</h2><span>Sora for words · JetBrains Mono for data only</span></div>
    <div class="ts">
      <div><code>hero · 500 · −0.045em · up to 96px</code><span style="font-weight:500;font-size:44px;letter-spacing:-0.045em;line-height:1">I build small companies.</span></div>
      <div><code>chapter · 300 · −0.035em</code><span style="font-weight:300;font-size:34px;letter-spacing:-0.035em;line-height:1.12">Everything my machines read, <span style="color:var(--ink-3)">kept.</span></span></div>
      <div><code>title · 500 · −0.025em</code><span style="font-weight:500;font-size:20px;letter-spacing:-0.025em">Conflict escalates financially before it turns military</span></div>
      <div><code>body · 300 · 17px / 1.7</code><span style="font-weight:300;font-size:17px">Reserve freezes and settlement bans arrive months ahead of any shooting. Lý tưởng càng lớn, kiểm chứng thực tế càng phải chặt.</span></div>
      <div><code>label · mono · 12px floor</code><span class="mono" style="font-size:11.5px;color:var(--ink-3)">2026.09.01 · analysis · rev 3 · <span style="color:var(--human)">2 notes from me</span></span></div>
    </div>

    <div class="sh" style="margin-top:44px"><h2>Space &amp; surface</h2><span>1px rules · 4–6px radii · no grid</span></div>
    <p class="lede" style="margin-bottom:24px">The ground is near-black with one static body of light, high and left. Rules are 1px; corners are 4–6px; there are no cards, no glass, no gradients on text, no background pattern. Depth comes from a single raised tone on hover and from scale.</p>
    <div class="sh"><h2>Kinds</h2><span>six kinds of reading, one glyph each</span></div>
    <div class="glyphs">{['news','breakdown','research','model','analysis','technical'].map(t => <span class="kind" set:html={glyph(t, 16) + '<em>' + t + '</em>'} />)}</div>

    <div class="sh"><h2>Motion</h2><span>ease-out quart · one authored moment per surface</span></div>
    <div class="mo">
      <button type="button" data-demo="count">replay: counters</button>
      <button type="button" data-demo="theme">flip theme</button>
    </div>
    <div class="intro" style="padding:20px 0 30px;position:relative" id="demo-line"><p style="margin:0;font-family:var(--mono);font-size:11.5px;color:var(--ink-3)">status <b class="num" data-count="712" style="color:var(--ink-2)">712</b> pages · <b class="num" data-count="7" style="color:var(--ink-2)">7</b> agents</p></div>
    <p class="lede">Grammar: transform and opacity first; scroll-linked reveals floored at 50% opacity so nothing is ever hidden; page changes crossfade in 180ms; numbers count up once to their real value; the hero lines land in sequence. Nothing in the background moves. <code class="mono">prefers-reduced-motion</code> turns every one of these off.</p>
  </div>

  <script>
    function bootKit() {
      const sw = document.getElementById('sw'); if (!sw) return;
      const c = document.createElement('canvas'); c.width = c.height = 1; const ctx = c.getContext('2d', { willReadFrequently: true })!;
      const hexOf = (v: string) => { ctx.fillStyle = getComputedStyle(document.documentElement).getPropertyValue(v).trim(); ctx.fillRect(0,0,1,1); const [r,g,b] = ctx.getImageData(0,0,1,1).data; return '#' + [r,g,b].map(x => x.toString(16).padStart(2,'0')).join(''); };
      const paint = () => sw.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-hex]').forEach(el => { el.textContent = `${el.textContent!.split(' · ')[0]} · ${hexOf(el.dataset.hex!)}`; });
      paint();
      new MutationObserver(paint).observe(document.documentElement, { attributes: true, attributeFilter: ['data-theme'] });
      document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-demo]').forEach(b => b.addEventListener('click', () => {
        const d = b.dataset.demo;
        if (d === 'theme') (document.getElementById('theme') as HTMLButtonElement)?.click();
        if (d === 'line') { const el = document.getElementById('demo-line')!; el.classList.remove('intro'); void el.offsetWidth; el.classList.add('intro'); }
        if (d === 'count') document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('#demo-line [data-count]').forEach(el => { const t = Number(el.dataset.count); const t0 = performance.now(); const tick = (n: number) => { const k = Math.min(1,(n-t0)/900); el.textContent = String(Math.round(t*(1-Math.pow(1-k,4)))); if (k<1) requestAnimationFrame(tick); }; requestAnimationFrame(tick); });
      }));
    }
    document.addEventListener('astro:page-load', bootKit);
  </script>
</Base>
